</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.07 16.53)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:32.61em;--ltx-fo-height:12.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="179" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 175.54)" width="451.23"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A8.p6.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:32.61em;">
<span id="A8.p6.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.p6.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">System:<span id="A8.p6.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span><pre id="A8.p6.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
You are a helpful Python coding assistant.
When given a programming problem, respond with self-contained
Python 3 code that solves the task and passes the provided tests.
Output only a single ‘‘‘python ...‘‘‘ code block with no additional
commentary.

Problem:
{problem}

Details:
{description}

Unit tests your solution must pass:
{tests}

Setup code that runs before the tests:
{setup}

Write the full solution now.
Remember to return only Python code inside a single fenced block.
</pre>
<span id="A8.p6.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.p6.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">User:<span id="A8.p6.pic1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> {PROBLEM}</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
